  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 206 PM MDT TUE JUL 28 2026\nWhile the four corners high begins to slip out of position\nFriday and Saturday, warming and drying will continue. Both days\nwill be the hottest in the forecast, with temperatures in lower\nelevations in the mid to upper 90s. Guidance indicates\ntemperatures around 100 degrees are possible if the smoke clears\nsome, although with southwest flow continuing this is unlikely.\nThe stalled British Columbia low begins to move inland Friday,\nand is set to bring a dry cold front through the area Saturday\nevening. With Saturday being the hottest day, this combination\nof heat, very dry conditions, and frontal gusty winds will lead\nto critical fire weather across the area. Behind the cold front,\nSunday will be 5-10 degrees cooler than Saturday, but dry and\ngusty conditions will remain, leading to continued elevated fire\nweather. Temperatures begin to climb again Monday and Tuesday as\nhigh pressure rebuilds over Nevada. Southwest flow resumes the\ntransport of hot and dry air early next week.",
